```
"name": "execute",
"parameters": {
  "properties": {
    "mode": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], ...},
    "request": {"anyOf": [{"additionalProperties": {}, "type": "object"}, {"type": "string"}], ...},
    "target": {"anyOf": [{"additionalProperties": {}, "type": "object"}, {"type": "string"}], ...}
  },
  "required": []
}
```

So request parameter can be either object or string. As an object, it's required to include the structure. As a string... hmm.

WAIT! Maybe the system is sending my request as a STRING when I want it as an OBJECT. And the framework sends `{mepty_string: ""}` as default since it can't be parsed as an object?

